  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/plc1100.html",
  "prefLabel": "Plc 1105.04 Expired License",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Plc 1105.04 Expired License.\n\n(a) If a complete application for renewal is not received until after the expiration date of the license, the license shall be expired.\n\n(b) An individual whose license has expired shall not practice in New Hampshire unless and until the license is reinstated within one year in accordance with Plc 312.\n\n(c) An individual whose license has lapsed who wishes to obtain a license in New Hampshire shall apply for an initial license in accordance with Plc 1104.02.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Plc 1100) #13391, eff 5-27-22; ss by #14444, eff 1-26-26, EXPIRES: 1-26-36 (formerly Plc 1105.05)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/plc1100.html"
